WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:01.723
- [Presenter] Legal Eagle is sponsored

00:00:01.723 --> 00:00:03.480
by CuriosityStream and Nebula.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.890
Get 26% off using the
link in the description.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.460
- (laughs) Liberals want
to evict an elderly,

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.970
financially troubled COVID
survivor and his family

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.620
from inner-city public housing.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.270
I mean, that's only a bad
take because it doesn't say

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.810
that the liberals also want to take away

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.547
that elderly COVID survivor's
healthcare as well.

00:00:21.547 --> 00:00:23.550
(upbeat drumbeats)

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.060
Well, we're finally on the other side

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.490
of an incredibly momentous election.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.600
But at times, it was
a little touch and go.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.000
And while we know the outcome now,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.860
along the way, there were some...

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:35.350
How do I put this charitably?

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.300
Bad election takes.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.630
But now that hindsight is 20/20,

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.490
why don't we engage in
a little schadenfreude

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:47.140
and let's make fun of some
really bad election opinions.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.720
Because not all election
opinions are created equal.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:51.553
So let's take a look

00:00:51.553 --> 00:00:53.621
at some of the worst
election takes out there.

00:00:53.621 --> 00:00:55.760
(dramatic percussion)

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.780
Yeah, so many of my friends
were completely thirsty

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.370
for chart-throb himself, Steve Kornacki

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:06.680
or Korsnacki, as I heard
him referred to many times.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.200
- [Leslie] Steve, you
are doing it for me doug.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.560
With these numbers.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.393
Wait a minute.

00:01:12.393 --> 00:01:14.010
- Let's take out the
old trusty calculator.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.085
- [Leslie] Did this mother
(bleep) just pull out a calc?

00:01:16.085 --> 00:01:19.320
(laughing) Steve, hey Steve, hey Steve,

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.010
you ain't gotta do it all, 'cuz.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:24.550
- I'm not in any place to opine on that.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.210
I'm not saying that Steve
Kornacki is not hot.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.670
What I am saying is that
lawyers are familiar

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.430
with a phenomenon called
the deposition effect.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:36.190
Deposition is where you're
stuck in the same room

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:38.400
for hours where you're
questioning a witness.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.970
There is opposing counsel
and the stenographer,

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:42.520
usually in the same room.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.300
Back when we could do
things in the same room

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.330
and it wasn't all virtual.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.440
And one of the effects of the deposition

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.270
is that because you're locked
in a room with that person,

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.774
multiple people for many hours at a time,

00:01:52.774 --> 00:01:56.520
you build up an affinity for these people.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.137
Whether it's opposing
counsel or the stenographer,

00:01:59.137 --> 00:02:01.510
and they might seem more attractive

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:03.460
than they did when you
first entered that room.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.050
Look, I'm not saying that that's the case

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:06.010
with Steve Kornacki

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:07.570
but I'm just saying, you know, sleep on it

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:11.318
and ask yourself if you still
feel that way in the morning.

00:02:11.318 --> 00:02:12.880
(laughing)

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.850
(dramatic percussion)

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:19.700
- We want the law to be
used in a proper manner.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.610
So we'll be going to
the U.S. Supreme Court.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.650
We want all voting to stop.

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:27.483
- [Host] All right,

00:02:27.483 --> 00:02:29.330
the king of bad election takes himself,

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.230
Donald Trump, saying that he's going to go

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:32.570
straight to the Supreme Court.

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:34.080
And I hate to break it to him

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.400
but as avid viewers of this channel know,

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.060
that's generally not
how these things work.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:41.400
The U.S. Supreme Court
is the highest court

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.220
in the federal system though
when it comes to state law,

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.280
often it is the state Supreme
Court that is the highest

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.630
and last word on the subject.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.270
But generally you don't go

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.100
straight to the United
States Supreme Court

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.230
and it can take a very,
very long time to get there.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.550
In fact, even when the
court is moving fast,

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:00.010
like we saw with Bush versus Gore in 2000,

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.280
it can take over a month

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.940
before it actually gets to the
United States Supreme Court.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:06.280
Though interestingly,
Donald Trump is not as off

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.430
as he usually is in this respect.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:11.160
Because occasionally under
extremely rare circumstances,

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:14.880
the court can weigh in on
emergency relief applications

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.160
and here Justice Alito did
issue an injunctive order

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.650
saying that the state of
Pennsylvania should follow

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:24.150
basically the guidance of the
secretary of the Commonwealth

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.396
which seems like everyone
was doing anyway.

00:03:26.396 --> 00:03:28.240
(dramatic percussion)

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.730
But of course, this
order from Justice Alito

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.880
on the Supreme Court
engendered its own bad take

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.790
in the form of this
tweet from Sean Spicer,

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:39.810
who is saying that basically
this order from Justice Alito

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:43.190
was a game changer and will
basically change the outcome

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:45.080
of the election in Pennsylvania.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.240
That's not how that happens.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.550
And in fact, it seems like
there are a very, very small

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:51.910
number of ballots that came in
after the statutory deadline

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:54.380
that might be in this small grace period

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.650
created by the courts.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.700
And in fact, it seems like
the state of Pennsylvania

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:58.690
was already doing it.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:00.290
That they were segregating the ballots,

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:01.280
they were counting the ballots

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.360
but not adding them to the
cumulative total for the state

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.450
and waiting for the courts

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:06.950
to figure out what they're going to do

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.660
with these provisional ballots.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:11.240
So, it's not going to change the outcome.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:12.292
Sorry, Sean Spicer.

00:04:12.292 --> 00:04:14.443
(dramatic percussion)

00:04:14.443 --> 00:04:16.243
- [Crowd] Stop the
counts! Count those votes!

00:04:16.243 --> 00:04:17.444
Stop the votes! Count those votes!

00:04:17.444 --> 00:04:19.032
Stop the count! Count those votes!

00:04:19.032 --> 00:04:21.800
Stop the count! Count those votes!

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:25.430
- Ah yes, who could forget
the near simultaneous chanting

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.010
from the crowds of Trump's supporters.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:28.380
Some saying to stop the count

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.960
and others saying that we
needed to count the votes.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.700
Look, they have a first amendment right

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:35.450
to protest the things that
they are aggrieved about.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:37.810
But at the same time it seems ironic

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.263
at the very least that they would,

00:04:39.263 --> 00:04:42.470
at least some would argue for
this anti-democratic measure

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:45.440
of stopping the counting
of the actual ballots,

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.380
or at least the processing of the ballots.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:48.553
Now, in fairness,

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.980
I think this is a little
bit blown out of proportion

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:54.020
because the laws of different
states are different.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:57.680
There is no universal election
law throughout this country.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.740
So what's legal in one state

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.590
might not be legal in another state.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:03.180
But still it's a bad look

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:05.810
when you're out there
protesting against the counting

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.220
of the votes themselves

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.170
while at the same time,

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:09.330
another group of Trump supporters

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.820
are arguing the exact opposite thing.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:12.787
Bad election take.

00:05:12.787 --> 00:05:15.230
(dramatic percussion)

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:18.130
Yeah, the pollsters got
this one pretty wrong.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.250
The polls showed that Joe
Biden was going to win

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.760
in a landslide and that the Democrats

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.370
were going to pick up
potentially many seats

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:27.790
in the Senate and take a
majority in the Senate.

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:29.920
And that of course never happened.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.380
The pollsters learned from
their mistakes in 2016,

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:35.800
where they were off by an average of 5%.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:38.020
They revised their models,
they did their homework

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.620
and in 2020, they were off by over 7%.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:43.800
Now, in fairness, they
did get some things right.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.630
Apparently Arizona and
Virginia are pretty close

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:49.050
to the way that the pollsters
predicted things would go.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.892
But across the country,
they were incredibly wrong.

00:05:51.892 --> 00:05:54.030
(dramatic percussion)

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:56.590
- The pollsters got it knowingly wrong.

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.160
They got it knowingly wrong.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:05:59.160
- [Host] Knowingly wrong?

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:01.290
As if they were doing everyone a favor

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.610
by suggesting that the Democrats

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:06.130
were going to win in a landslide.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.840
You could argue it both ways I suppose.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.650
That it might suppress the votes

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:11.450
or people might not go out and vote

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.580
because they think that it's
going to be a landslide.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.400
That's what some people say about 2016.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:16.460
But...(laughs).

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.310
But there's no doubt
that the polls in general

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.688
saying that it was going
to be a complete bloodbath

00:06:21.688 --> 00:06:23.226
we're very wrong.

00:06:23.226 --> 00:06:25.430
(dramatic percussion)

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:26.680
I feel like I would be remiss

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:31.680
if I didn't include a QAnon
as a world-class bad take

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:36.850
because I'm sorry, the military
didn't get operationalized.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.510
As far as I know, all
my friends were not sent

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:43.040
to Guantanamo Bay and Q
has been incredibly silent

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:46.480
now that Trump is no longer
going to be re-elected.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:47.313
You know, frankly,

00:06:47.313 --> 00:06:49.710
I miss good old fashioned
conspiracy theories

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:51.530
that were harder to debunk.

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:53.320
They weren't making pronouncements

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:56.630
about what would and would
not happen on certain days.

00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:58.230
It could easily be disproven.

00:06:58.230 --> 00:06:59.830
I miss the old conspiracy theories

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:01.610
like the black helicopters
and the chemtrails.

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:04.830
I mean, those were at least general enough

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:08.120
that there was no certainty that things

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:09.510
were not gonna happen.

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:10.900
QAnon needs to try harder.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.120
It sad that they got the
election so, so wrong

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.880
and that no one is in jail.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.930
(dramatic percussion)

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.870
Ah, a Donald Trump tweet from 2012

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.410
where he says the electoral
college is a disaster

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:23.530
for democracy.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:26.140
I guess this is a bad
take with respect to him

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.520
losing the election in this year.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.360
But I actually, I think
that's absolutely right.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:32.620
The electoral college is
a disaster for democracy

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.980
just because the popular
vote happened to line up

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:37.930
with the electoral college vote in 2020

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.700
does not mean that it's
a good institution.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:43.680
And then there are all kinds
of anti-democratic issues

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:44.550
with the electoral college.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:46.910
I've covered that in
several videos in the past.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:48.870
But frankly, given the
fact that it's possible

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:51.080
that faithless electors
could screw up the results

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:55.750
and how the votes are
wildly disproportionate,

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.697
the electoral college
definitely needs some work.

00:07:58.697 --> 00:08:01.068
(dramatic percussion)

00:08:01.068 --> 00:08:03.770
(laughs)This is probably
the funniest thing

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:06.560
that has ever happened
in American politics,

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:07.393
probably full stop.

00:08:07.393 --> 00:08:09.780
Because it was not the case
that the Trump administration

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:10.990
was holding a press conference

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:13.720
at the Four Seasons Hotel in Philadelphia.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.600
The Four Seasons tweeted out that in fact,

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.470
they were not holding the
press conference there.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:19.480
And then Trump surrogates mobilized

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:22.440
and held a press conference
in front of Four Seasons'

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:25.970
total landscaping in a
rundown industrial part

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:27.920
of Philadelphia, just on a whim.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:29.280
Credit where credit is due.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:32.130
They got their stuff together
and held a press conference

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:34.750
in a place that should not
have had a press conference.

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:38.620
In between a crematorium
and an adult sex toy store.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:39.980
You literally could not make that up.

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:41.570
If the writers had written that for Veep,

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:43.790
they would have rejected it as too crazy.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:46.090
- You know what? I kinda love it.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:48.070
- Probably the funniest
thing that has ever happened

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:49.266
in American politics ever.

00:08:49.266 --> 00:08:51.466
(dramatic percussion)

00:08:51.466 --> 00:08:53.911
- [Crowd] Fox News sucks!

00:08:53.911 --> 00:08:57.820
- And they're actually
chanting Fox News sucks.

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.060
Fox news sucks.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:00.010
The reason why they're chanting

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:05.010
that is because Fox news called
Arizona for Biden yesterday.

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:09.330
And a lot of people are angry about that.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:11.080
- It's incredible that so
many people on the right

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:15.650
were apoplectic that Fox news
called Arizona for Joe Biden.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:17.930
Now, granted it was
early on in the process

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:20.560
but it couldn't have had
any effect on the election.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.640
They didn't call it until
after the polls were closed.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.610
As it turns out, Fox news was right.

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:29.450
So, obviously the damage could
not have actually existed

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:32.980
because it turns out that
Arizona did go for Joe Biden.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.170
But that's the irony

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:36.715
of the facts don't care
about your feelings crowd.

00:09:36.715 --> 00:09:39.263
(dramatic percussion)

00:09:39.263 --> 00:09:41.250
Pat, to me, the Senator from Pennsylvania,

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:43.560
as well as others were
rightfully complaining

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.730
that Pennsylvania didn't start counting

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:50.260
the mailed in ballots and other
ballots until election day.

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:53.360
And thus the counting
process in Pennsylvania

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:54.760
was long and drawn out.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.280
And that's, that's perfectly fine.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.190
But the reason it was long

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:00.150
and drawn out is because of state law.

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:03.060
State law mandated that
they couldn't start counting

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:03.900
those ballots.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.380
A lot of other states, including Florida,

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.860
start way ahead of time so that
they don't have this backlog

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:12.480
of ballots that are uncounted

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:15.180
and that they can stretch out
until long after election day.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:16.660
And in Pennsylvania,

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:19.530
it was a Republican
house of representatives

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:22.530
that refused to pass
legislation to change that law.

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:24.930
We're all exasperated
about how long it takes

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.800
in all the different states,
including Pennsylvania,

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.270
but you've got to change the
law to be able to handle that.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.460
And under COVID,

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:32.020
you would think that they
would want to do that,

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.202
but of course they did not.

00:10:33.202 --> 00:10:35.163
(dramatic percussion)

00:10:35.163 --> 00:10:37.710
(laughs) Liberals want
to evict an elderly,

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:39.480
financially troubled COVID survivor

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:41.870
and his family from
inner-city public housing.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.450
I mean, that's only a bad take

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.400
because it doesn't say that the liberals

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:48.820
also want to take away that
elderly, COVID survivor's

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:49.934
healthcare as well.

00:10:49.934 --> 00:10:51.930
(dramatic percussion)

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:54.100
And back to Donald Trump quoting

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:56.810
the illustrious former
acting attorney general,

00:10:56.810 --> 00:10:57.757
Matthew Whitaker.

00:10:57.757 --> 00:10:58.710
"We need an explanation

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:00.130
as to how these numbers have been running

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:01.970
up for the last two or three days."

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.670
Well, that seems pretty simple.

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:06.470
Number one, the president
said people should not vote

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.350
by mail.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:10.440
Democrats often said that
they should vote by mail.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.470
The vote by mail tends
to favor the Democrats

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:13.303
in the first place.

00:11:13.303 --> 00:11:16.960
And of course there's the
issue that when another vote

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:19.440
comes in, that adds to the counts.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:20.730
That's called math.

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:23.010
And on top of that, the count continues.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:26.440
So as a lot of people were pointing out,

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:28.670
on election day we're not
going to have a final count.

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:30.760
So it takes a long time
to process these things.

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:32.380
And lots of states have laws

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:34.820
that say that as long as
the ballot is postmarked

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:35.790
by election day,

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:39.670
that the ballot itself can come
in many days or weeks later

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:40.730
and still be counted.

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:42.465
So, that's the answer.

00:11:42.465 --> 00:11:44.527
(dramatic percussion)

00:11:44.527 --> 00:11:47.300
"No state authority nor FEC
has yet to declare the winner

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:50.250
yet Fox News just called
it for Joe Biden, wow."

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:52.540
Yeah, that's sort of how that works.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.210
The calling of a presidential election

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:56.100
is mainly just a media thing.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:12:00.800
The FEC doesn't make the call
nor does Fox News in general.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:01.900
That's sort of just a projection.

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:04.570
Doesn't actually carry any
legal weight with it, so.

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:06.820
Rudy Giuliani was also
saying that the court

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:09.190
would have to decide
who was the president.

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:10.710
That's also not how that works.

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:12.350
The court might decide the lawsuits,

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:14.080
which is probably what he was hinting at,

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.870
but it's not for a court to declare anyone

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:18.240
the president or not.

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:21.940
It's just a media thing that
they say based on the results

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:23.426
that who's the projected winner.

00:12:23.426 --> 00:12:25.327
(dramatic percussion)

00:12:25.327 --> 00:12:27.320
"Funny how CNN has suddenly stopped

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:30.187
it's "COVID COVID, COVID
COVID!" drumbeat, isn't it?"

00:12:30.187 --> 00:12:31.020
(scoffs)

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:33.410
Maybe my timeline is just
different from other people's.

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:36.100
But my timeline on Twitter,
at least, was filled

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.500
with so many people talking

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:42.500
about 110, 120, 130,000
new COVID cases a day.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.130
Exactly the same time
that they were talking

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:44.963
about the election.

00:12:44.963 --> 00:12:47.710
And of course the election
is relatively consequential

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:48.670
for COVID.

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:51.500
So it makes sense that
COVID was sort of crowded

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.320
out for like a day or two.

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:56.596
COVID never left my timeline
and I'm still stuck at home.

00:12:56.596 --> 00:12:58.750
(dramatic percussion)

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.640
Ben Shapiro arguing
every legally cast vote

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:01.473
should be counted.

00:13:01.473 --> 00:13:02.970
Every illegally cast vote should not.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:03.803
End of story.

00:13:03.803 --> 00:13:05.540
Well, everyone agrees with that,

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:07.830
but a lot of the litigation itself,

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.670
or at least the posturing
over the litigation

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:12.890
is over what is considered
a legal vote or not.

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.800
You could make the same argument in 2000

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:15.770
in Bush versus Gore

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.560
but when you're talking about the law

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:19.760
about whether it permits a recount or not,

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:21.120
or whether a hanging chad

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:24.460
or a vote made with a marker versus a pen

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:26.000
is legally cast or not,

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.000
you're changing the rules as with respect

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.080
to what is legally cast or not.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:32.900
So, that's sort of the
beginning of the fight

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:34.493
not the end of the fight.

00:13:34.493 --> 00:13:36.720
